== global 4's Bit[547] under --reach
NAME.reached: bit:547 0 in both readings. s17 holds bit:547 = 0. No action of either file writes bit:547, none has bit:547 = {1} in
its precondition (10531 actions of the input_settled file have bit:547 = {0}), and none reads var:182 (reached 0 and above).
So the fork at global 4's [0000] runs only its bit:547 = 0 side; the other side, with var:182's fork under it, is held and never freed.
The writes that make bit: a fact (an indexed Bit write whose index does not fold) are the machine's unknown-target writes: left out of
the record's effects and listed on it (machine.rs `put`, builder.rs), with or without --reach.
actorroom:6 is reached at -1, 0 and 28; 72 is not (F1c's gate had 28, 72, 0 and not known).
sentence(7,320): 6 actions and 6 frozen with reach; with input_settled also [202] 30 and 30 frozen, [14] 3 and 3 frozen (78).
The 30 of [202]: actorroom:6 = -1 12, = 28 12, = 0 6; all bit:547 = {0}.

