== the optimal cost from s17, on taskcore's SAS files of both (FD's search memory limit 2 GB, 1800 s, nice 10, the memory guard on)
| task | operators | A* landmark cost partitioning (lm_rhw) | greedy ff, bound 8 |
| --reach, input_settled | 43323 | h0 6; f = 6 not closed in 1800 s, peak 1427 MB; no plan | cost 7, 7 steps, 0.5 s search |
| full, input_settled | 44839 | h0 6; f = 6 not closed in 1800 s, peak 1430 MB; no plan | cost 7, 7 steps, 0.5 s search |
| --reach, without input_settled | 17672 | h0 7, plan cost 7, 8 expanded | |
The cost-7 plans, both: event(local:211@33), fold:walk_to(316)[202], event(script:2@736), event(local:218@16), sentence(9,566),
event(script:2@736) (a fold of 2 in the full file's), event(script:2@915).
So the optimal cost is 6 or 7 on both; A* did not decide which. A greedy search with bound 7 (a plan of cost 6) on the --reach task
found none in 600 s. That is no proof.
Other admissible searches tried on the --reach task: landmark cost partitioning over lm_merged(lm_rhw, lm_zg): the same 28 landmarks,
h0 6; lm_zg alone: no h0 in 60 s; lm_exhaust, lmcut and the three stubborn-set prunings: conditional effects not supported. The FD
build has no LP solver, so no optimal cost partitioning.

